WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:07.130
Welcome back. We've explored a
lot of data together so far.

2
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.436
In the National Data tab,
we looked at demographics,

3
00:00:10.436 --> 00:00:14.739
community living and participation,
and work and economic information.

4
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:20.740
In the City Data tab, we zoomed in to see
similar information at the local level.

5
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.869
These tabs showed us
numbers in percentages.

6
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.411
They told us how many
people with disabilities

7
00:00:28.411 --> 00:00:31.179
fit into certain categories or topics.

8
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.029
Now, we're gonna build
on that information and

9
00:00:34.029 --> 00:00:36.789
knowledge to explore
something a little different.

10
00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.720
Instead of just counting people with
disabilities, we're going to look at scores.

11
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.622
These scores grade states on how well
people with disabilities are doing.

12
00:00:46.622 --> 00:00:48.232
We call these scorecards.

13
00:00:48.232 --> 00:00:52.870
Now, let's navigate to the Scorecards
tab at the top corner of the page.

14
00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:56.100
Let's click on National Scorecard.

15
00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.444
A scorecard is ADA-PARC's
way of ranking states.

16
00:01:01.444 --> 00:01:06.139
It shows how well people with
disabilities are doing in each state.

17
00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:07.638
Think of it like a grade.

18
00:01:07.638 --> 00:01:11.089
States with higher scores are
doing better at making sure people

19
00:01:11.089 --> 00:01:14.379
with disabilities can participate
equally in their community.

20
00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:18.892
It's a quick way to find
which states are leaders,

21
00:01:18.892 --> 00:01:21.069
and which states need improvement.

22
00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:26.597
Let's look at the national scorecards.
Here, there are three scorecards.

23
00:01:26.597 --> 00:01:29.500
Community participation, Community Living.

24
00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.649
And work and economics.

25
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.430
Additionally, you can find
scorecards on each state.

26
00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:39.884
In a previous video, we
looked at national data,

27
00:01:39.884 --> 00:01:43.099
and there were a lot of
topics in each category.

28
00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:47.396
In community participation, we
looked at health insurance coverage,

29
00:01:47.396 --> 00:01:52.240
high school graduation rates, having a
college degree, and access to technology.

30
00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:57.082
To create a scorecard, we take all
of these individual pieces of data,

31
00:01:57.082 --> 00:01:59.780
like health insurance
and graduation rates.

32
00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.889
Then, we combine them into one score.

33
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:08.870
States where people with disabilities do
well across more topics get higher scores.

34
00:02:09.449 --> 00:02:12.495
States where people with
disabilities do not

35
00:02:12.495 --> 00:02:15.680
do as well in multiple
areas get lower scores.

36
00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:21.478
We're basically adding up outcomes
across all these different areas.

37
00:02:21.478 --> 00:02:27.199
These scorecards help us compare
disability data easily in between states.

38
00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:30.981
So instead of looking at 20 different data

39
00:02:30.981 --> 00:02:33.905
points like we did in
the National Data tab,

40
00:02:33.905 --> 00:02:39.420
you can find which states are doing well
overall at a glance in the Scorecards tab.

41
00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:42.040
Let's go over what these scores mean.

42
00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.090
Let's scroll down.

43
00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:49.860
Each scorecard has a map and a key that
tells you exactly what these colors mean.

44
00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:56.599
These keys change based on each category,
like community participation and living.

45
00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.954
However, they all have the same
four key categories: poor, subpar,

46
00:03:02.954 --> 00:03:08.699
good, and excellent, which you can
find at the bottom of the map.

47
00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.355
We want to see darker colors.

48
00:03:11.355 --> 00:03:15.439
This represents higher opportunities
for people with disabilities.

49
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:19.759
Now that we understand
what scorecards are.

50
00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.989
Let's explore the Community
Participation Scorecard.

51
00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.502
The Community Participation
Score is a state average of all

52
00:03:27.502 --> 00:03:31.117
of the variables in the Community
Participation category,

53
00:03:31.117 --> 00:03:35.620
such as access to insurance,
transportation, technology, and education.

54
00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.720
We want to see that states have opportunities
to participate in the community.

55
00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.060
Let's look at the map and its key.

56
00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:46.232
As we said, each map has four categories,

57
00:03:46.232 --> 00:03:49.305
ranging from poor, subpar,
good, and excellent.

58
00:03:49.305 --> 00:03:53.164
And just like before, darker
colors mean more of something.

59
00:03:53.164 --> 00:03:56.565
In this case, darker colors
means a higher score and

60
00:03:56.565 --> 00:03:59.770
more opportunity to
participate in the community.

61
00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:05.725
This means that people with
disabilities are doing better in those

62
00:04:05.725 --> 00:04:09.233
darker states when it comes to
participating in the community.

63
00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:11.157
We can see that in the West Coast,

64
00:04:11.157 --> 00:04:15.740
there are several states that earn the
highest score for community participation.

65
00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:21.254
We can see that comparatively in the
South there are more lighter colors,

66
00:04:21.254 --> 00:04:23.140
like in Texas for example.

67
00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.436
So we know that there are
fewer opportunities for

68
00:04:26.436 --> 00:04:29.409
community participation
compared to the West Coast.

69
00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:34.160
To find more specific information, we
can scroll down to the data tables.

70
00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:39.770
In each data table, it'll tell you
the ranking on the left-hand side.

71
00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.729
Next to that, it's tier, so
those different key categories.

72
00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:51.179
the state and the community participation
score. So this will be the overall score.

73
00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:55.569
of those categories to the
right of that. So it's average.

74
00:04:56.390 --> 00:05:01.349
And this is ranked from the highest state
or territory all the way to the lowest.

75
00:05:01.349 --> 00:05:04.410
You can explore this
information on your own time.

76
00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.620
Below this table.

77
00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.812
we can see the top and bottom performers.

78
00:05:09.812 --> 00:05:13.073
So you can see the top 5
highest performers and the

79
00:05:13.073 --> 00:05:16.206
top bottom performers in
community participation,

80
00:05:16.206 --> 00:05:19.979
and what the range is between
the top and bottom performer.

81
00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:24.361
Below this, we can see the
average score by census region,

82
00:05:24.361 --> 00:05:28.560
so the Northeast, West, Midwest,
and South, like we compared before.

83
00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:34.039
Below, you can see the definitions of
some of these terms that we've reviewed.

84
00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:37.579
Alright, let's scroll
all the way to the top.

85
00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.240
And let's change the category.

86
00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:43.300
To do so, you'll go under Category.

87
00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:48.940
And you'll click on Community Living.
And then next you'll click on Generate.

88
00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.960
Sometimes, these scorecards can take

89
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.178
15 to 25 seconds to generate. That's
because there's a lot of data.

90
00:05:57.178 --> 00:05:59.460
So hang tight in the meantime.

91
00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:03.444
While we're waiting, we can go
over how to download a page.

92
00:06:03.444 --> 00:06:06.647
Next to that generate button,
you can click on download.

93
00:06:06.647 --> 00:06:09.049
So this way you can take this information.

94
00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.609
Alright, we can scroll down.

95
00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:16.341
At the top of each page, it'll give
you a brief look on who is the

96
00:06:16.341 --> 00:06:20.500
highest score out of the states and
territories, and who's the lowest score.

97
00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:24.481
Alright, so let's look
at community living.

98
00:06:24.481 --> 00:06:27.542
Community living represents
the level of opportunity

99
00:06:27.542 --> 00:06:32.369
for people with disabilities to live in
the community, rather than an institution.

100
00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:36.792
Previously, we discussed that
there are two types of living.

101
00:06:36.792 --> 00:06:42.170
Living in the community, so living at home
or a non-institutionalized group quarter.

102
00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:47.079
Or, in an institution, which can be a
nursing home or correctional facility.

103
00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:50.118
Since higher scores mean good outcomes,

104
00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:54.439
this scorecard shows us where more
people are living in the community.

105
00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.870
We want to see that people
with disabilities have greater

106
00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:01.470
opportunities to live in the
community rather than an institution.

107
00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:04.514
So in this map, we can
see that once again,

108
00:07:04.514 --> 00:07:08.540
the western region has more darker
colors and higher opportunities,

109
00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:11.365
and the southern region
have lighter colors and

110
00:07:11.365 --> 00:07:14.069
lower opportunities to
live in the community.

111
00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:19.039
Take a look at the key below the map, and
it'll tell you the exact specific ranges.

112
00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:23.410
One thing to note is that
scores range from 0 to 100.

113
00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.760
In this specific map,

114
00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:31.949
we can see that the highest performing
state is 79.2 and the lowest is 24.8.

115
00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.200
Okay.

116
00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:37.508
We have that same data table
that you can take a look at.

117
00:07:37.508 --> 00:07:40.930
I'm going to show you how to find
a specific state or territory.

118
00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.443
So in this top box, we're
going to click on it,

119
00:07:43.443 --> 00:07:46.330
and we're going to type the
state that we want to see,

120
00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:47.934
and then it's going to pop up.

121
00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:51.410
That way, you don't have to spend
time looking through the table.

122
00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:56.271
I encourage you to look through
this information on your own time,

123
00:07:56.271 --> 00:07:58.219
and explore the state that you live.

124
00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.543
Okay, let's scroll to the top.

125
00:08:01.543 --> 00:08:05.434
We're going to do the same thing
and start to look at work and

126
00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:09.450
economics by clicking under category
and generate the scorecard.

127
00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.323
So I'm going to get
started talking about work

128
00:08:12.323 --> 00:08:14.400
and economics while we
wait for this to load.

129
00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:17.566
So remember from the national data tab,

130
00:08:17.566 --> 00:08:22.100
work and economics includes things
like living below the poverty line,

131
00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:25.339
being employed, and not
being burdened by housing.

132
00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.126
Since higher scores mean good outcomes,

133
00:08:28.126 --> 00:08:32.369
we're measuring where people with
disabilities are doing well economically.

134
00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:37.690
We can see that Utah has the highest score,
so they're doing the best economically,

135
00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:39.098
whereas in Puerto Rico,

136
00:08:39.098 --> 00:08:43.934
people with disabilities have the lowest
opportunities to do well economically.

137
00:08:43.934 --> 00:08:45.770
Let's scroll down to this map.

138
00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:49.850
We can see that a new heat
map has been generated.

139
00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.695
Overall, just looking at it, I can
see that there's a lot more states

140
00:08:53.695 --> 00:08:57.235
that are represented by these darker
colors, which is a good thing.

141
00:08:57.235 --> 00:08:59.349
This means that there's more people with

142
00:08:59.349 --> 00:09:01.779
disabilities doing well
overall, economically.

143
00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:04.742
Alright, we can scroll down,

144
00:09:04.742 --> 00:09:08.161
and I encourage you to look
through the data table and find

145
00:09:08.161 --> 00:09:11.290
any states or territories
that are interesting to you.

146
00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:16.003
Okay, we have one last topic to discuss.

147
00:09:16.003 --> 00:09:20.679
Let's scroll to the top and
click on State Scorecards.

148
00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.679
Right now, it's currently
auto-generated to look at Illinois,

149
00:09:25.679 --> 00:09:29.939
but to change it, you'll click on State
or Territory, you can look up the

150
00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:34.789
area that you're interested in, and
then click on Generate Scorecard.

151
00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.249
We'll wait for this to load.

152
00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:46.583
Alright, there we go.

153
00:09:46.583 --> 00:09:52.040
At the top of each page, there is a scale
that shows the state score out of 100.

154
00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:55.726
Below that, it shows the ranking of each

155
00:09:55.726 --> 00:09:59.310
state in each category
and the overall score.

156
00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:03.919
So, to find more specific data in each
category, we can scroll down below.

157
00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:09.625
We can find information
about community living.

158
00:10:09.625 --> 00:10:12.897
So we can find Illinois
score and then below it,

159
00:10:12.897 --> 00:10:17.193
it'll show us the US average for
community living, which is 50.

160
00:10:17.193 --> 00:10:19.306
So we can see that in Illinois,

161
00:10:19.306 --> 00:10:23.329
they rank they have a lower
score compared to other states.

162
00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:28.424
And then you can find specific
information about community living,

163
00:10:28.424 --> 00:10:30.569
as well as community participation,

164
00:10:30.569 --> 00:10:33.939
work and economics, and then
we have the score summary.

165
00:10:33.939 --> 00:10:37.370
So this just gives you all of
those scores in one place.

166
00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:42.710
And below, you can find some
definitions of these categories.

167
00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:45.960
Let's scroll back to the top.

168
00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:49.819
Let's click on New to
Scorecard, Start Here.

169
00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:54.691
So this is going to provide you
information about what scorecards are,

170
00:10:54.691 --> 00:11:00.039
how they're generated and built, how we
calculate that data, and what they measure.

171
00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:04.733
So, let's recap what we've covered.

172
00:11:04.733 --> 00:11:08.409
In the National Data tab,
we explored demographics,

173
00:11:08.409 --> 00:11:12.661
community living and participation,
and work and economics.

174
00:11:12.661 --> 00:11:16.770
In the City Data, we zoomed
in to find local information.

175
00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:20.769
Now, in Scorecards, we've learned
how to find state rankings and

176
00:11:20.769 --> 00:11:25.040
compare how well people with disabilities
are doing across the country.

177
00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:28.942
You've learned how to read
heat maps, interpret tables,

178
00:11:28.942 --> 00:11:33.016
and understand what the data means
for people with disabilities.

179
00:11:33.016 --> 00:11:34.290
So, congratulations!

180
00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:38.555
You've now learned everything you
need to use the ADA-PARC website.

181
00:11:38.555 --> 00:11:40.720
